CLASS MedalUnlockQueue
    DESCRIPTION: Durable buffer of medal unlocks that were requested but never confirmed, plus the background pass that retries them
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    NOTE: This is a hand-written class that does NOT extend BaseObject

    PURPOSE: A medal unlock is a single request, and a request can go missing. The connection
    drops partway through, the server is down, or the player closes the tab before the response
    comes back. In every one of those cases the player has already earned the medal.

    WHY NOT AN IN-MEMORY QUEUE?: The thing that lost the request is usually the same thing that
    ended the page. So ids are written to STORAGE before the request goes out, and cleared only
    once the gateway has actually ruled on them.

    OWNERSHIP: Core creates one of these in its constructor, the same way it creates AppState.
    That is what scopes the buffer correctly: the pending set belongs to one App ID, and Core is
    the per-app instance, so a static singleton would be wrong the moment two Cores run for two
    different projects.

    CADENCE: NGIO owns the retry timer and nothing else, exactly as it does for keepAlive(): it
    holds the timer, and the work happens down here. See NGIO.retryPendingMedalUnlocks() and
    NGIO.startMedalUnlockRetryTimer().

    DEPENDENCIES: The generated models, Errors, and Core (which it uses to send each unlock).

    ====================
    PROPERTIES
    ====================

    PUBLIC keepGuestUnlocks: Boolean
        PURPOSE: Whether an unlock attempted while nobody is signed in is kept and sent once a
        player signs in
        WHY: The usual case wants it: a player earns a medal before signing in, signs in, and
        gets it. Some games hand out their own reward to signed-out players and must never see
        a medal follow later. When false, a signed-out unlock is never recorded, and guest
        entries already stored are dropped by the next retry pass instead of sent.
        DEFAULT: true
        NOTE: NGIO exposes this as NGIO.keepGuestMedalUnlocks.

    PUBLIC holdGuestUnlocks: Boolean
        PURPOSE: Whether guest entries wait for the game to claim or discard them, instead of
        going to whoever signs in next
        WHY: On a shared device the next player to sign in may not be the one who earned the
        medal. With this on, the game can ask the player whether the medals are theirs, then
        call claimGuestUnlocks() or discardGuestUnlocks() with the answer.
        DEFAULT: false
        NOTE: Has no effect while keepGuestUnlocks is false, since no guest entry is kept then.
        NGIO exposes this as NGIO.holdGuestMedalUnlocks.

    PRIVATE core: Core
        PURPOSE: The Core instance this queue belongs to
        WHY: Used to send each Medal.unlock, to read who is signed in, and to scope the storage
        key by App ID

    PRIVATE storageKey: String
        PURPOSE: A unique key used to avoid naming collisions when saving the pending list
        WHY: Storage keys MUST contain the App ID. Apps hosted on the same host share a storage
        space, so an unqualified key collides across every game using this library there. Same
        reasoning as AppState.sessionStorageKey.
        DEFAULT: "ngio-pending-medal-unlocks-for-" + core.appId

    PRIVATE inFlight: Set of Integer
        PURPOSE: The ids currently out on a live request, foreground or retry
        WHY: Lets a background pass skip anything already being sent instead of firing a
        duplicate request for the same id
        DEFAULT: Empty
        NOTE: In memory only. This describes right now, not something that has to survive a
        reload, so unlike the pending list it is deliberately NOT persisted.

    PRIVATE retryListeners: Array of { listener: Function, thisArg: Object }
        PURPOSE: Everything that asked to hear about retry passes
        WHY: Retries run on a timer, with nobody waiting on a callback. Without this, a game
        has no way to learn that a medal earned while the connection was down has now unlocked.
        DEFAULT: Empty

    ====================
    OUTCOME STATUS
    ====================

    COMMENT: Every outcome this class reports carries a status: where the attempt left the
    COMMENT: medal. Callers need it because "error is not null" covers three very different
    COMMENT: situations: the gateway refused the medal for good, the medal is still buffered and
    COMMENT: will be sent again, or it was never kept. Define these as constants, under the
    COMMENT: name MedalUnlockStatus, in whatever form the language favors.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT:   UNLOCKED = "unlocked"  The gateway unlocked it.
    COMMENT:   REJECTED = "rejected"  The gateway ruled on this medal and refused it (202 above
    COMMENT:                          all). It is not retried.
    COMMENT:   PENDING  = "pending"   Not ruled on yet, and still buffered: a retry pass will
    COMMENT:                          send it again.
    COMMENT:   HELD     = "held"      Earned while nobody was signed in, and buffered until the
    COMMENT:                          game claims or discards it (holdGuestUnlocks).
    COMMENT:   DROPPED  = "dropped"   Not ruled on, and not buffered either: a guest unlock with
    COMMENT:                          keepGuestUnlocks off. Nothing will send it again.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: error is null exactly when status is UNLOCKED.

    ====================
    WHOSE UNLOCK IS IT
    ====================

    COMMENT: The buffer lives in local storage, so on a shared device (family PC, school lab,
    COMMENT: expo kiosk) it outlives the player who filled it. With plain ids, a medal player A
    COMMENT: earned offline would be sent the next time ANYONE signed in, and player B would get
    COMMENT: it. So every stored entry is { id: Integer, user: Integer or null }, where user is
    COMMENT: the id of the player who earned it, or null if nobody was signed in.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT:   - A player's entry is sent only while that player is signed in. Signing out does
    COMMENT:     not drop it; it waits for them.
    COMMENT:   - A guest entry (user null) is sent for whoever is signed in, and settled for them.
    COMMENT:     With holdGuestUnlocks on, it waits for claimGuestUnlocks() instead.
    COMMENT:   - When the gateway rules on an id for a player, drop that player's entry for the
    COMMENT:     id AND any guest entry for it. Leave other players' entries alone.

    ====================
    CONSTRUCTOR
    ====================

    FUNCTION constructor(core: Core)
        PARAMETERS:
            core: (required) The Core instance that owns this queue

        BEHAVIOR:
            SET this.core TO core
            SET this.storageKey TO "ngio-pending-medal-unlocks-for-" + core.appId
            SET this.inFlight TO an empty set
            SET this.retryListeners TO an empty list
    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    PUBLIC METHODS
    ====================

    FUNCTION getPendingIds(): Array of Integer
        PURPOSE: Lists the medal ids currently recorded as requested but not yet ruled on, for
        any player

        RETURNS: An array or list of medal ids without duplicates, empty when nothing is pending

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN the id of each entry in this.readEntries(), with duplicates removed
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getGuestIds(): Array of Integer
        PURPOSE: Lists the medal ids recorded while nobody was signed in, and not yet sent or
        discarded

        RETURNS: An array or list of medal ids without duplicates, empty when there are none

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN the id of each entry in this.readEntries() whose user is null, with
                duplicates removed
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION claimGuestUnlocks(ids: Array of Integer, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Hands guest entries to the signed-in player and sends them

        PARAMETERS:
            ids: (required) The medal ids to claim. Ids with no guest entry are ignored.
            callback: Function to call once every claimed id has come back, as callback(outcomes)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback

        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            outcomes: The same shape unlock() reports, one entry per id that was sent

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE user AS this.currentUserId()
            CREATE entries AS this.readEntries()
            CREATE claimed AS the ids in ids, with duplicates removed, that have an entry in
                entries whose user is null

            IF user is null OR claimed is empty THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING an empty list
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: Re-own each claimed entry BEFORE sending it, for the same reason unlock()
            COMMENT: records before sending. One that can't be sent yet then waits for this
            COMMENT: player like any of their own, and the retry pass sends it despite the hold.
            REMOVE every entry with user null and an id in claimed FROM entries
            FOR EACH id IN claimed
                IF entries has no entry with this id AND this user THEN
                    ADD { id: id, user: user } TO entries
                END IF
            END FOR
            CALL this.write(entries)

            CREATE toSend AS claimed minus anything in this.inFlight
            IF toSend is empty THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING an empty list
                RETURN
            END IF
            CALL this.send(toSend, user, callback, thisArg)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION discardGuestUnlocks(ids: Array of Integer)
        PURPOSE: Drops guest entries for these ids without sending them

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE entries AS this.readEntries()
            CREATE kept AS the entries that do NOT have user null and an id in ids
            IF kept has as many entries as entries THEN
                RETURN
            END IF
            CALL this.write(kept)

        NOTE: Players' own entries are never touched, even for the same id.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION unlock(ids: Array of Integer, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Unlocks one or more medals, recording each id before it is sent

        PARAMETERS:
            ids: (required) The medal ids to unlock
            callback: Function to call once every id has come back, as callback(outcomes)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback

        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            outcomes: One entry per id, each holding id, the unlocked medal (or null), an error
                      (or null), and a status (see OUTCOME STATUS). error is null exactly when
                      status is UNLOCKED.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE unique AS ids with duplicates removed
            IF unique is empty THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING an empty list
                RETURN
            END IF

            CREATE user AS this.currentUserId()

            COMMENT: Record every id as pending BEFORE sending anything. It might look as
            COMMENT: though a medal that fails against a healthy gateway should never have been
            COMMENT: buffered at all - do NOT restructure it that way. Writing before the send
            COMMENT: is what makes a crash or reload mid-request survivable. An id that fails
            COMMENT: against a healthy gateway sits here for a few milliseconds, costing nothing.
            IF user is not null OR this.keepGuestUnlocks is true THEN
                CALL this.addPending(unique, user)
            END IF

            CALL this.send(unique, user, callback, thisArg)

        NOTE: A fresh unlock ALWAYS sends immediately. Nothing here waits on the retry pass.
        The background pass exists only to recover requests an earlier attempt never got
        confirmation for.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION retryPending(callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Re-sends what is still pending for whoever is signed in now: their own entries
        and any guest entries. Another player's entries wait until that player signs in again.
        With holdGuestUnlocks on, guest entries wait for claimGuestUnlocks() instead.

        PARAMETERS:
            callback: (optional) Function to call once this pass is done, as callback(outcomes)
            thisArg: Context to use when calling the callback

        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            outcomes: The same shape unlock() reports, one entry per id sent. An empty list when
                      nothing was waiting.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE pending AS an empty list
            CREATE user AS null
            TRY
                CREATE entries AS this.readEntries()

                IF this.keepGuestUnlocks is false AND any entry in entries has user null THEN
                    REMOVE every entry with user null FROM entries
                    CALL this.write(entries)
                END IF

                SET user TO this.currentUserId()
                SET pending TO the ids of the entries whose user equals user, plus those
                    whose user is null when this.holdGuestUnlocks is false, with duplicates
                    removed, minus anything in this.inFlight
            CATCH
                COMMENT: This NEVER throws and never reports a failure. A pass that cannot reach
                COMMENT: the gateway is exactly the case it exists to tolerate, and one bad pass
                COMMENT: must not stop later ones from running.
                SET pending TO an empty list
            END TRY

            IF pending is empty THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING an empty list
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: send(), not unlock(): these are already recorded, and must not be
            COMMENT: recorded again under whoever happens to be signed in now.
            CALL this.send(pending, user, FUNCTION onPassComplete(outcomes)
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING outcomes
                COMMENT: Loop over a COPY, so a listener that removes itself mid-loop does not
                COMMENT: make the next one get skipped.
                FOR EACH { listener, thisArg } IN a copy of this.retryListeners
                    CALL listener WITH context thisArg PASSING outcomes
                END FOR
            END FUNCTION, null)

        NOTE: Safe to call by hand, for instance on an application-level "back online" event.
        NOTE: Listeners hear only passes that sent something. A pass with nothing waiting is
        not news.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION addRetryListener(listener: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Asks to hear about every retry pass that sends anything, as listener(outcomes),
        whether the timer or the game started it

        PARAMETERS:
            listener: (required) Function to call with each pass's outcomes
            thisArg: Context to use when calling it

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.retryListeners already has an entry with this listener and this thisArg THEN
                RETURN
            END IF
            ADD { listener: listener, thisArg: thisArg } TO this.retryListeners

        NOTE: This is how a game hears that a medal earned while the connection was down has
        now unlocked: look for outcomes whose status is UNLOCKED. NGIO exposes this as
        NGIO.addMedalRetryListener().
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION removeRetryListener(listener: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Stops a listener added with addRetryListener(), matched by listener and thisArg

        BEHAVIOR:
            REMOVE the entry with this listener and this thisArg FROM this.retryListeners, if any
    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    PRIVATE METHODS
    ====================

    FUNCTION send(ids: Array of Integer, user: Integer or null, callback: Function, thisArg: Object)
        PURPOSE: Sends one Medal.unlock per id on behalf of user, and settles the buffer as each
        comes back

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE outcomes AS an empty list
            CREATE remaining AS the length of ids

            FOR EACH id IN ids
                ADD id TO this.inFlight

                COMMENT: One request per medal, NOT one batch. The gateway rules on each medal
                COMMENT: separately, and Core's component queue is shared with the game, so a
                COMMENT: background pass must never drain it.
                CALL this.core.callComponent("Medal.unlock", { id: id }, FUNCTION onComplete(response)
                    REMOVE id FROM this.inFlight

                    CREATE outcome AS this.adjudicate(id, response)
                    IF outcome.adjudicated is true THEN
                        COMMENT: The gateway ruled on this medal for this player. Its fate is
                        COMMENT: settled and retrying cannot change it, so drop it whether the
                        COMMENT: answer was yes or no.
                        CALL this.removePending(id, user)
                    END IF

                    ADD { id: id, medal: outcome.medal, error: outcome.error,
                        status: this.statusFor(outcome, user) } TO outcomes
                    SET remaining TO remaining - 1
                    IF remaining is 0 AND callback is defined THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING outcomes
                    END IF
                END FUNCTION, this)
            END FOR
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION statusFor(outcome: Object, user: Integer or null): String
        PURPOSE: Decides where an answered attempt left the medal. See OUTCOME STATUS.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF outcome.adjudicated is true THEN
                IF outcome.error is null THEN
                    RETURN UNLOCKED
                END IF
                RETURN REJECTED
            END IF

            COMMENT: Not ruled on, so the answer is whatever the buffer still holds. A guest
            COMMENT: entry counts as well as one for user: a retry pass sends guest entries for
            COMMENT: whoever is signed in, and they stay stored as guest entries until ruled on.
            CREATE entry AS the first entry in this.readEntries() with this outcome's id and
                a user that is null or equal to user
            IF there is no such entry THEN
                RETURN DROPPED
            END IF
            IF entry.user is null AND user is null AND this.holdGuestUnlocks is true THEN
                RETURN HELD
            END IF
            RETURN PENDING
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION currentUserId(): Integer or null
        PURPOSE: The signed-in player's user id, or null when nobody is signed in

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.core.appState.session.user is null THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF
            RETURN this.core.appState.session.user.id
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION readEntries(): Array of { id: Integer, user: Integer or null }
        PURPOSE: Reads the stored pending entries

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CREATE raw AS STORAGE_GET(this.storageKey)
                IF raw is null OR raw is empty THEN
                    RETURN an empty list
                END IF

                CREATE parsed AS JSON_DECODE(raw)
                IF parsed is not a list THEN
                    RETURN an empty list
                END IF

                CREATE entries AS an empty list
                FOR EACH item IN parsed
                    IF item is a number THEN
                        COMMENT: A bare id is an entry from before entries recorded their
                        COMMENT: player. Read it as a guest entry rather than lose it.
                        ADD { id: item, user: null } TO entries
                    ELSE IF item is an object AND item.id is a number THEN
                        ADD { id: item.id, user: item.user if it is a number, otherwise null } TO entries
                    END IF
                END FOR
                RETURN entries
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Unparseable stored data is treated as ABSENT, not fatal. Corrupt local
                COMMENT: state must degrade to "nothing pending", never crash an unlock.
                RETURN an empty list
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION adjudicate(id: Integer, response: Response): Object
        PURPOSE: Decides whether the gateway actually ruled on this specific medal

        RETURNS: An object holding id, medal, error, and adjudicated

        WHY: The buffer exists to survive connectivity failures, and NOTHING else. So the
        question to ask of every outcome is not "did this succeed?" but "has the gateway ruled
        on this specific medal?" If it has, retrying cannot change the answer.

        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT: What came back                              | Ruled on? | Action
        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT: No response at all                          | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A response, but success is not true         | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A per-medal result that succeeded           | Yes       | DROP
        COMMENT: A per-medal failure on 102/104/110/111      | No        | KEEP
        COMMENT: A per-medal failure on anything else (202)  | Yes       | DROP
        COMMENT: ------------------------------------------------------------------------

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Nothing reached the gateway, or nothing came back.
            IF response is null OR response has no getResult method THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: an error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            COMMENT: The envelope was rejected before this medal was considered.
            IF response.success is not true THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: response.error OR an error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            CREATE result AS response.getResult()
            IF result is null THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: an "invalid response" error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            IF result.success is true THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: result.medal, error: null, adjudicated: true }
            END IF

            CREATE error AS result.error OR an "invalid response" error
            CREATE code AS error.code

            COMMENT: Session-class codes mean the call was blocked on identity before the medal
            COMMENT: was looked at, so it is NOT adjudicated.
            IF code is 102 OR code is 104 OR code is 110 OR code is 111 THEN
                RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: error, adjudicated: false }
            END IF

            COMMENT: Anything else means the gateway looked at this medal and rejected it, 202
            COMMENT: (INVALID_MEDAL_ID) above all. A medal id that no longer exists, or was
            COMMENT: mistyped, or was removed from the game is dropped on the first response
            COMMENT: that reaches the gateway and never retries again.
            RETURN { id: id, medal: null, error: error, adjudicated: true }

        NOTE: The session-class row is NOT an exception to the rule. Medal.unlock requires a
        login, so an unlock attempted while signed out is refused LOCALLY by
        BaseComponent.getPreflightError() and never sent, with code 102 or 110. That refusal is
        deliberately built to be indistinguishable from a server refusal, so you cannot tell
        where it came from. You do not need to: discriminating on the error CLASS puts the local
        refusal in the keep set for free, which is the right outcome. A player who earns a medal
        as a guest and signs in later should still get it, unless keepGuestUnlocks is false.

        NOTE: With this rule there is no retry cap, no attempt counter, and no maximum age, and
        none of them are needed. Nothing can retry indefinitely except a genuine connectivity
        failure, which is exactly what should.
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION addPending(ids: Array of Integer, user: Integer or null)
        PURPOSE: Records ids as pending, owned by user

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE entries AS this.readEntries()
            FOR EACH id IN ids
                IF entries has no entry with this id AND this user THEN
                    ADD { id: id, user: user } TO entries
                END IF
            END FOR
            CALL this.write(entries)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION removePending(id: Integer, user: Integer or null)
        PURPOSE: Drops the entries for id owned by user, and any guest entry for id

        WHY: A guest unlock sent after a sign-in is settled for that player. Other players'
        entries for the same id still wait for them.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE entries AS this.readEntries()
            CREATE kept AS the entries that do NOT have this id with user null or equal to user
            IF kept has as many entries as entries THEN
                RETURN
            END IF
            CALL this.write(kept)
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION write(entries: Array of { id: Integer, user: Integer or null })
        PURPOSE: Persists the pending list, always as entries, never as bare ids

        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                CALL STORAGE_SET(this.storageKey, JSON_ENCODE(entries))
            CATCH
                COMMENT: Best-effort durability, never fatal. Quota limits, private browsing,
                COMMENT: and storage disabled by the user are all real, and none of them should
                COMMENT: turn an unlock into an error.
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS
